What CropGuard is

A lightweight multi-task model for tomato leaf disease, built to run on a phone
8-class classification: healthy, bacterial_spot, early_blight, late_blight, leaf_mold, mosaic_virus, septoria_leaf_spot, yellow_leaf_curl_virus
2-channel segmentation: lesion mask + leaf mask
Severity = lesion_px / leaf_px, computed analytically from the masks (not learned)
Detection was ruled out of scope; corpus: /home/logiclocus/tmp/cgpack/cropguard_v7_split (train 715 / val 156 / test 150; PlantDoc 79 held for classification-only eval)

How we implemented it

Model (2.53M params, INT8-friendly)
fasternet_t0 (pretrained, ImageNet) → features at 4 scales [40,80,160,320] → BiFPNLite neck (width 96) → BilinearDecoder (progressive 80→160→320, Hardswish; finest features stride-4) → 2 lesion/leaf logits at 320×320 → LesionGatedClassificationHead (features gated by the detached lesion mask) → 8-class logits.

Training (v8 recipe)
Loss = cls CE (inverse-√ class weights capped 3×, label smoothing 0.05) + seg_loss_v7 (lesion: BCE pos_weight=20 + 3× Focal-Tversky α=0.3 β=0.7 γ=1.33; leaf: BCE+Dice with −1 sentinel exclusions)
AdamW lr 5e-4, wd 1e-4, cosine warmup 450/10800 steps, grad clip 10, AMP, EMA 0.999, batch 8 @ 320px, seed 1337
Staged gates: dataset-hash gate → 8-image memorization gate → 102 epochs training (55-min Kaggle cap) → val summary. Checkpoint selection = val macro-F1 (tie-break lesion IoU)
PlantDoc test untouched until item 4

Where it stands (measured): cls macro-F1 0.68 (raw, epoch 35); lesion segmentation broken (val IoU ~0.04-0.05, flat for 102 epochs, area over-prediction 3-89×); severity worse than the constant baseline (0.1026 vs 0.0384).

What was actually wrong — found today

The architecture was never the main problem. *The lesion masks in the corpus are 1-pixel polygon outlines, not filled regions.

Raw evidence
chk_maskthick.py -> frac of pixels surviving 3x3 erosion: mean=0.000 (all 635 lesioned masks)
chk_maskstats.py -> median 181 connected components/mask @320, largest comp p50 = 25px
constant-blob ceiling IoU on val = 0.0000 (no pixel is lesion in >50% of images)
ASCII dump: 1-px open curves, e.g. ".....#..................."
SOURCE: prepare_plantseg.py:97-118 poly_to_mask() walked polygon EDGES
        vertex-to-vertex, 1px per step — interior never filled
Consequence: the model was trained to reproduce lacy scribbles — impossible at stride-4 resolution — so it converged to a diffuse haze (that's the flat 0.04 IoU and the "over-prediction"). The 8-image gate only "passed" because it memorized 8 scribble patterns. Severity labels were a perimeter/leaf ratio (p50 0.0125), not area ratio. Boxes were outline fragments.

